WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:02.901
-Welcome, everybody.
Welcome, welcome, welcome

00:00:02.901 --> 00:00:05.567
to "The Tonight Show,"
everybody. You're here.

00:00:05.567 --> 00:00:07.234
You made it.
Thank you for watching at home.

00:00:07.234 --> 00:00:08.701
Thanks for being here.
Yeah, welcome.

00:00:08.701 --> 00:00:10.601
Enjoy yourself.

00:00:10.601 --> 00:00:13.033
Well guys,
I want to wish everyone

00:00:13.033 --> 00:00:15.167
a happy Martin Luther King Jr
Day.

00:00:15.167 --> 00:00:19.901
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:19.901 --> 00:00:21.334
It's such an important holiday.

00:00:21.334 --> 00:00:23.367
And of course, leaders
from all across the country

00:00:23.367 --> 00:00:24.734
have put out statements.

00:00:24.734 --> 00:00:25.934
President Biden said...

00:00:32.834 --> 00:00:34.334
Vice President Harris said...

00:00:38.634 --> 00:00:40.300
Congressman George Santos
said...

00:00:46.801 --> 00:00:48.067
-Aww.
-So that was nice.

00:00:48.067 --> 00:00:51.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:51.234 --> 00:00:55.300
Meanwhile, today, Biden spoke
in an event honoring MLK,

00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:57.434
and Dr. King's daughter-in-law
was there.

00:00:57.434 --> 00:00:58.901
It was actually her birthday.

00:00:58.901 --> 00:01:01.300
So, Biden decided to sing
to her.

00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:02.934
Let's see how that went.

00:01:02.934 --> 00:01:04.701
-On somebody's birthday,
you sing happy birthday.

00:01:04.701 --> 00:01:09.300
You ready?
♪ Happy birthday to you ♪

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:12.767
♪ Happy birthday to you ♪

00:01:12.767 --> 00:01:16.000
♪ Happy birthday dear...
[ Mumbles ] ♪

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:17.434
[ Laughter ]

00:01:17.434 --> 00:01:20.133
♪ Happy birthday to you ♪

00:01:20.133 --> 00:01:23.167
[ Laughter ]

00:01:24.968 --> 00:01:26.834
-First rule -- first rule.

00:01:26.834 --> 00:01:28.334
Don't start singing
"Happy Birthday"

00:01:28.334 --> 00:01:30.167
unless you know
the person's name.

00:01:30.167 --> 00:01:31.801
[ Laughter ]

00:01:31.801 --> 00:01:34.434
Yeah, that must have been
real special for [mumbles].

00:01:34.434 --> 00:01:36.300
[ Laughter ]

00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:38.801
There's a reason why the
birthday song at TGI Fridays

00:01:38.801 --> 00:01:41.033
doesn't have the name in it.

00:01:41.033 --> 00:01:42.400
Rookie move, Joe.

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:44.133
Every singer knows
that when you forget the lyric,

00:01:44.133 --> 00:01:45.901
that's when you point the mic
towards the crowd.

00:01:45.901 --> 00:01:48.434
It's like,
♪ Happy birthday, dear... ♪

00:01:48.434 --> 00:01:50.434
[ Laughter ]

00:01:50.434 --> 00:01:52.868
♪ Happy birthday ♪
And you do that.

00:01:52.868 --> 00:01:54.634
I mean, come on. Alright.
Let's give him a break.

00:01:54.634 --> 00:01:56.467
It's not like Biden's done this
before.

00:01:56.467 --> 00:01:59.701
-♪ Happy birthday, [mumbles] ♪

00:01:59.701 --> 00:02:02.400
♪ Happy birthday to you ♪

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:07.234
[ Laughter ]

00:02:07.234 --> 00:02:09.067
-Oh. [ Laughs ]

00:02:09.067 --> 00:02:11.367
-Yep, Biden spoke
for 30 minutes.

00:02:11.367 --> 00:02:13.300
When he wasn't belting out
"Happy Birthday,"

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:15.701
he was doing that
weird whispering thing again.

00:02:15.701 --> 00:02:17.367
Which brings us
to the latest installment of

00:02:17.367 --> 00:02:19.834
"Joe Biden: Whisperer in Chief."

00:02:19.834 --> 00:02:22.934
♪♪

00:02:22.934 --> 00:02:26.300
-You know, all these new IRS
agents we have is because

00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:28.167
[whispering] they fired
a lot of them.

00:02:28.167 --> 00:02:32.234
If any of these bills
happen to reach my desk,

00:02:32.234 --> 00:02:33.734
[whispering] I will veto them.

00:02:33.734 --> 00:02:36.300
I think the highest individual
loan was 1.2 million

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:39.100
or something. [Whispering] I
didn't hear a word.

00:02:39.100 --> 00:02:42.100
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:44.868 --> 00:02:47.100
-[Whispering] He's the best.

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:48.567
[Normally] Speaking of Biden,
over the weekend,

00:02:48.567 --> 00:02:51.467
five more pages of classified
documents were found

00:02:51.467 --> 00:02:53.200
at his home in Delaware.

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:54.868
Yep, this year,
instead of an Easter egg hunt,

00:02:54.868 --> 00:02:56.400
they're going to send the kids
over to Biden's home

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:57.567
to look for more documents.

00:02:57.567 --> 00:02:59.701
It's like,
"Found one under the sofa."

00:02:59.701 --> 00:03:01.200
"Alright, hand it over."

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:03.734
At this point, they've found
documents in so many places,

00:03:03.734 --> 00:03:05.133
it's like we're playing Clue.

00:03:05.133 --> 00:03:07.634
It's like North Korea's
nuclear codes in the garage

00:03:07.634 --> 00:03:10.534
with the Corvette.
Yeah, I got it!

00:03:10.534 --> 00:03:12.267
Yup, the scandal has gotten
so big, today,

00:03:12.267 --> 00:03:14.734
Hunter Biden told his dad,
"I can't be seen with you

00:03:14.734 --> 00:03:16.767
right now."

00:03:16.767 --> 00:03:19.634
Hey, I saw that Johnson &amp;
Johnson has recently scaled back

00:03:19.634 --> 00:03:22.400
production on
their COVID vaccine.

00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:24.100
That's like Hooters saying
that they're taking

00:03:24.100 --> 00:03:25.701
kale chips off the menu.

00:03:25.701 --> 00:03:28.734
[ Laughter ]

00:03:28.734 --> 00:03:30.934
"No kale chips?
I'll just get 50 wings."

00:03:30.934 --> 00:03:32.334
[ Laughter ]

00:03:32.334 --> 00:03:34.100
Well, this is cool --
I read that the latest Gen Z

00:03:34.100 --> 00:03:36.467
obsession is using flip phones.

00:03:36.467 --> 00:03:40.434
Yeah, tons of young adults
are buying flip phones

00:03:40.434 --> 00:03:42.667
I think it's great.
I used to love my flip phone.

00:03:42.667 --> 00:03:45.667
-Oh, yeah.
You love your flip phone?

00:03:45.667 --> 00:03:47.300
What else?

00:03:47.300 --> 00:03:49.367
-What else?
I mean, I like flip phones.

00:03:49.367 --> 00:03:51.667
I like flying drones.

00:03:51.667 --> 00:03:55.501
-That's cool. What else?

00:03:55.501 --> 00:03:57.801
-I like hot scones.
I like garden gnomes.

00:03:57.801 --> 00:03:58.968
I like watching
"Game of Thrones,"

00:03:58.968 --> 00:04:00.200
"Home Alone," and "Yellowstone"

00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:02.868
on my own with an ice cream cone
in Bayonne.

00:04:02.868 --> 00:04:05.501
I like hair combed, beard full
grown, and riding the cyclone

00:04:05.501 --> 00:04:08.067
with Tommy Lee Jones, reading
poems covered in cologne.

00:04:08.067 --> 00:04:10.133
I like Ray Brone,
I like Carl Malone,

00:04:10.133 --> 00:04:12.601
ozone, singing baritone
while Sly Stallone

00:04:12.601 --> 00:04:14.701
plays trombone
and Roman Grosjean chaperones

00:04:14.701 --> 00:04:16.567
about clones and overdue loans.

00:04:16.567 --> 00:04:18.300
But you know what I really love?

00:04:18.300 --> 00:04:19.334
-Who?

00:04:19.334 --> 00:04:21.367
-The Rolling Stones.
2, 3...

00:04:21.367 --> 00:04:27.734
♪ [ Singing indistinctly ] ♪

00:04:27.734 --> 00:04:30.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:31.501 --> 00:04:33.701
Well, guys, there's a lot
of pop culture news right now.

00:04:33.701 --> 00:04:35.968
"Avatar 2" is doing great
at the box office.

00:04:35.968 --> 00:04:38.200
The new season of "The Bachelor"
starts next week.

00:04:38.200 --> 00:04:39.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:39.367 --> 00:04:41.467
Sarah Jessica Parker was just
seen filming

00:04:41.467 --> 00:04:44.601
the "Sex and the City" spin off
with the actor who plays Aiden.

00:04:44.601 --> 00:04:47.367
There's gonna be a sequel
to the horror movie "M3GAN."

00:04:47.367 --> 00:04:50.167
-Wait a second.
-What is it, Mark?

00:04:50.167 --> 00:04:52.334
-Did you just say
that Sarah Jessica Parker,

00:04:52.334 --> 00:04:54.968
A.K.A. Carrie Bradshaw, was
spotted filming

00:04:54.968 --> 00:04:58.067
the "Sex and the City" spin-off
A.K.A. "And Just Like That"

00:04:58.067 --> 00:05:02.434
alongside the actor who plays
Aiden, A.K.A. John Corbett?!

00:05:02.434 --> 00:05:03.834
-Yeah, I did.

00:05:03.834 --> 00:05:05.434
And here's the photo.

00:05:05.434 --> 00:05:06.901
Yeah.
-Wow.

00:05:06.901 --> 00:05:08.734
Aiden is coming back
in Carrie's life.

00:05:08.734 --> 00:05:11.267
That's big.
Pun intended.

00:05:11.267 --> 00:05:13.000
Who else is coming back?

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:14.901
What about her old boyfriend,
Patrick?

00:05:14.901 --> 00:05:16.234
-I'm not really sure.

00:05:16.234 --> 00:05:17.801
-Well, what about Burger?

00:05:17.801 --> 00:05:18.901
-I don't know.

00:05:18.901 --> 00:05:20.467
-How about Howie?

00:05:20.467 --> 00:05:21.901
-I have no idea.

00:05:21.901 --> 00:05:23.968
-What about Kurt, John, Jake,
or Ray?

00:05:23.968 --> 00:05:25.467
-Couldn't tell you.

00:05:25.467 --> 00:05:29.267
-What about Wade, Keith, Seth,
Jeremy, Sam, Bill, or Jeremiah?

00:05:29.267 --> 00:05:30.467
-I really don't know.

00:05:30.467 --> 00:05:32.701
-Okay. Well, what about Shawn,
Vaughn, Dr. Brad,

00:05:32.701 --> 00:05:34.934
Ben, Joe, or Alexander?

00:05:34.934 --> 00:05:36.234
-Beats me.

00:05:36.234 --> 00:05:38.868
-How about John, Jordan, Jason,
Tucker, or Parker?

00:05:38.868 --> 00:05:40.567
-Mark, I don't know.

00:05:40.567 --> 00:05:42.467
-I made up those last five.

00:05:42.467 --> 00:05:44.167
You're useless.

00:05:44.167 --> 00:05:46.567
Look, if you're not going
to give us any answers,

00:05:46.567 --> 00:05:47.801
we're out of here.

00:05:47.801 --> 00:05:50.167
Come on, guys.

00:05:50.167 --> 00:05:53.167
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:53.167 --> 00:05:56.334
♪♪

00:06:02.300 --> 00:06:04.400
-And just like that,
he was gone.

00:06:04.400 --> 00:06:06.701
[ Laughter ]

00:06:06.701 --> 00:06:08.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:08.601 --> 00:06:12.267
Hey, guys, I heard that LG
is recalling their 86-inch

00:06:12.267 --> 00:06:15.634
smart TVs because they can
tip over and trap people.

00:06:15.634 --> 00:06:16.968
[ Light laughter ]

00:06:16.968 --> 00:06:21.167
"Trap?" You know the LG people
went on thesaurus.com

00:06:21.167 --> 00:06:23.100
like, "What's a better word
than 'crush?'

00:06:23.100 --> 00:06:25.033
Trap."

00:06:25.033 --> 00:06:26.033
[ Laughter ]

00:06:26.033 --> 00:06:27.901
Trapped?

00:06:27.901 --> 00:06:29.667
Hey, guys, on Friday night,
somebody in Maine

00:06:29.667 --> 00:06:32.667
won the $1.3 billion
Mega Millions jackpot.

00:06:32.667 --> 00:06:34.167
And get this --
it's the first time someone

00:06:34.167 --> 00:06:36.267
has won the prize in Maine.

00:06:36.267 --> 00:06:38.067
In fact, the state is so excited
they're considering

00:06:38.067 --> 00:06:40.300
changing their
official welcome sign.

00:06:40.300 --> 00:06:41.501
Right now it says...

00:06:43.334 --> 00:06:44.367
But they might change it to...

00:06:47.300 --> 00:06:49.033
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:49.033 --> 00:06:50.901
Yeah.

00:06:53.033 --> 00:06:54.133
But they're also considering...

00:06:58.067 --> 00:07:01.200
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:01.200 --> 00:07:02.567
And finally, there is...

00:07:04.167 --> 00:07:06.434
That's what I'm talking about.

00:07:08.567 --> 00:07:09.968
Well, listen to this --
a new survey found

00:07:09.968 --> 00:07:12.868
that four out of five people
would work on vacation

00:07:12.868 --> 00:07:15.767
if it meant they could
have a longer trip.

00:07:15.767 --> 00:07:17.534
And Biden said, "Take it
from me, you're better off

00:07:17.534 --> 00:07:19.033
leaving your work at work."
Yeah.

00:07:19.033 --> 00:07:22.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:22.367 --> 00:07:25.167
And finally, guys, it is Monday,
the start of a brand-new week,

00:07:25.167 --> 00:07:26.934
and I think we all could use
a little encouragement

00:07:26.934 --> 00:07:28.734
to get things going
on the right foot.

00:07:28.734 --> 00:07:31.133
With that in mind, it's time
for some Monday Motivations.

00:07:31.133 --> 00:07:32.300
Here we go.

00:07:32.300 --> 00:07:33.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:33.400 --> 00:07:35.834
-♪ Monday motivations ♪

00:07:35.834 --> 00:07:39.467
♪♪

00:07:39.467 --> 00:07:42.434
-Hey, your hair looks
great today.

00:07:42.434 --> 00:07:46.767
[ Applause ]

00:07:46.767 --> 00:07:48.601
You're going to have
an amazing week.

00:07:48.601 --> 00:07:52.000
[ Applause ]

00:07:52.000 --> 00:07:53.968
When you're fishing
and you throw one back,

00:07:53.968 --> 00:07:56.133
its swims over to its friends
like, "Guys, it happened!

00:07:56.133 --> 00:07:57.400
I finally met Andrew."

00:07:57.400 --> 00:08:00.868
[ Applause ]

00:08:00.868 --> 00:08:02.701
When you zone out
waiting for your pizza rolls,

00:08:02.701 --> 00:08:06.033
your microwave is like, "OMG,
is he looking at me?"

00:08:06.033 --> 00:08:09.601
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:08:09.601 --> 00:08:12.801
Your JV soccer coach still talks
about that goal you made.

00:08:12.801 --> 00:08:14.067
Well, almost made.

00:08:14.067 --> 00:08:17.234
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:08:17.234 --> 00:08:19.267
When you sit down next to
someone on an airplane,

00:08:19.267 --> 00:08:22.701
they're like, "Jackpot.
Hello, future husband."

00:08:22.701 --> 00:08:25.934
[ Applause ]

00:08:25.934 --> 00:08:27.567
You didn't hear it,
but one time,

00:08:27.567 --> 00:08:30.033
your favorite teacher
accidentally called you son.

00:08:30.033 --> 00:08:33.667
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:08:33.667 --> 00:08:36.734
And finally, the gym turned you
away on January 1st

00:08:36.734 --> 00:08:40.300
because they didn't want to give
people unrealistic expectations.

